{"id": "JAH-RUGS-000001", "slug": "rug-signature", "title": "Persian Rugs", "edition": "signature", "src": "signature-generated-completion", "built_by": "assistant-built", "record_kind": "rug record", "ladder_rank": 1, "body": "Signature-original. Persian rugs are hand-knotted pile rugs made in Iran, prized for intricate designs and natural dyes. Famous weaving centers include Tabriz, Kashan, Heriz, and Qom, each with a recognizable style. Quality is measured partly by knot density: fine rugs can exceed 300 knots per square inch (KPSI). Designs feature medallions, floral all-over patterns, and geometric tribal motifs. A genuine hand-knotted Persian rug is woven on a loom, never glued, and its pattern shows clearly on the back.", "capabilities": ["Name the major Persian weaving centers", "Explain knot density (KPSI)", "Describe common Persian rug motifs", "Distinguish hand-knotted from machine-made rugs", "Explain why natural dyes matter"], "demo": {"language": "javascript", "title": "Knot density math", "code": "const w=60,h=90,kpsi=300;const knots=w*h*kpsi/1;J({knots_millions:+(w*h*kpsi/1e6).toFixed(1)});assert(w*h*kpsi===1620000,'knots');", "verified_output": "{\"knots_millions\":1.6}", "verified_at": "2026-10-21", "node": "v24.20.0", "run": "node"}, "provenance": {"source_paste": "manons-orders-2026-10-20-database-batch.txt (items 129-131) + field-audit fill", "last_verified": "2026-10-21", "origin": "assistant-built"}, "million_march": {"target": 1000000, "records_now": 8, "status": "march-in-progress"}, "generator": {"hard_cap": 1000000000000000, "ladder": ["simple", "competitive", "mix-and-match", "unmade", "top-notch-or-better", "future-grade", "god-mode"], "self_regulation": true, "stop_when_complete": true}, "ai": {"name": "Signature Rug Creator", "scope": "archive-aware", "assistant_maker": true}, "links": {"related": ["Oriental Rugs", "Area Rugs", "Runner Rugs"], "sibling_edition": "rug"}}
{"id": "JAH-RUGS-000002", "slug": "rug-signature", "title": "Oriental Rugs", "edition": "signature", "src": "signature-generated-completion", "built_by": "assistant-built", "record_kind": "rug record", "ladder_rank": 2, "body": "Signature-original. Oriental rugs are hand-knotted rugs from Turkey, the Caucasus, Central Asia, India, and China as well as Persia. Turkish rugs often use bold geometric designs and the symmetrical Turkish (Ghiordes) knot. Caucasian rugs are known for tribal patterns and strong colors. Indian rugs frequently copy Persian designs at lower prices. Chinese rugs often feature simpler, open designs with more empty field space.", "capabilities": ["List the regions that produce Oriental rugs", "Compare the Turkish and Persian knots", "Describe Caucasian rug style", "Explain Indian reproduction rugs", "Describe Chinese rug design traits"], "demo": {"language": "javascript", "title": "Knot-type comparison", "code": "const knots=[{n:'Turkish',sym:true},{n:'Persian',sym:false}];J({count:knots.length,symmetric:knots.filter(k=>k.sym).map(k=>k.n)});assert(knots.length===2,'knottypes');", "verified_output": "{\"count\":2,\"symmetric\":[\"Turkish\"]}", "verified_at": "2026-10-21", "node": "v24.20.0", "run": "node"}, "provenance": {"source_paste": "manons-orders-2026-10-20-database-batch.txt (items 129-131) + field-audit fill", "last_verified": "2026-10-21", "origin": "assistant-built"}, "million_march": {"target": 1000000, "records_now": 8, "status": "march-in-progress"}, "generator": {"hard_cap": 1000000000000000, "ladder": ["simple", "competitive", "mix-and-match", "unmade", "top-notch-or-better", "future-grade", "god-mode"], "self_regulation": true, "stop_when_complete": true}, "ai": {"name": "Signature Rug Creator", "scope": "archive-aware", "assistant_maker": true}, "links": {"related": ["Persian Rugs", "Area Rugs", "Runner Rugs"], "sibling_edition": "rug"}}
{"id": "JAH-RUGS-000003", "slug": "rug-signature", "title": "Area Rugs", "edition": "signature", "src": "signature-generated-completion", "built_by": "assistant-built", "record_kind": "rug record", "ladder_rank": 3, "body": "Signature-original. Area rugs are large rugs that cover part of a floor, typically under furniture groupings. Standard sizes include 5x8, 8x10, and 9x12 feet. A living-room rug should be large enough that at least the front legs of sofas and chairs rest on it. Under a dining table, the rug should extend at least 24 inches beyond the table on all sides so chairs stay on it. Use a rug pad underneath to prevent slipping and to add cushioning.", "capabilities": ["List standard area rug sizes", "Explain living-room rug placement rules", "Explain dining-room rug sizing", "Describe what a rug pad does", "Explain how to choose rug size for a room"], "demo": {"language": "javascript", "title": "Rug size for dining table", "code": "const table=[48,72];const ext=24;const rug=[table[0]+2*ext,table[1]+2*ext];J({rug_in:rug});assert(rug[0]===96&&rug[1]===120,'diningrug');", "verified_output": "{\"rug_in\":[96,120]}", "verified_at": "2026-10-21", "node": "v24.20.0", "run": "node"}, "provenance": {"source_paste": "manons-orders-2026-10-20-database-batch.txt (items 129-131) + field-audit fill", "last_verified": "2026-10-21", "origin": "assistant-built"}, "million_march": {"target": 1000000, "records_now": 8, "status": "march-in-progress"}, "generator": {"hard_cap": 1000000000000000, "ladder": ["simple", "competitive", "mix-and-match", "unmade", "top-notch-or-better", "future-grade", "god-mode"], "self_regulation": true, "stop_when_complete": true}, "ai": {"name": "Signature Rug Creator", "scope": "archive-aware", "assistant_maker": true}, "links": {"related": ["Persian Rugs", "Oriental Rugs", "Runner Rugs"], "sibling_edition": "rug"}}
{"id": "JAH-RUGS-000004", "slug": "rug-signature", "title": "Runner Rugs", "edition": "signature", "src": "signature-generated-completion", "built_by": "assistant-built", "record_kind": "rug record", "ladder_rank": 4, "body": "Signature-original. Runner rugs are long, narrow rugs made for hallways, entryways, and alongside beds. Common widths are 2 to 3 feet, with lengths from 6 to 14 feet. In a hallway, leave a few inches of bare floor on each side so the runner looks centered. Low-pile runners are best for high-traffic areas because they lie flat and are easy to clean. Outdoor runners made of synthetic fibers handle porches and patios.", "capabilities": ["Give common runner rug dimensions", "Explain hallway runner placement", "Explain why low pile suits high traffic", "Describe outdoor runner materials", "Explain bedside runner use"], "demo": {"language": "javascript", "title": "Runner centering", "code": "const hall=36,runner=27;const margin=(hall-runner)/2;J({hall_in:hall,runner_in:runner,margin_in:margin});assert(margin===4.5,'center');", "verified_output": "{\"hall_in\":36,\"runner_in\":27,\"margin_in\":4.5}", "verified_at": "2026-10-21", "node": "v24.20.0", "run": "node"}, "provenance": {"source_paste": "manons-orders-2026-10-20-database-batch.txt (items 129-131) + field-audit fill", "last_verified": "2026-10-21", "origin": "assistant-built"}, "million_march": {"target": 1000000, "records_now": 8, "status": "march-in-progress"}, "generator": {"hard_cap": 1000000000000000, "ladder": ["simple", "competitive", "mix-and-match", "unmade", "top-notch-or-better", "future-grade", "god-mode"], "self_regulation": true, "stop_when_complete": true}, "ai": {"name": "Signature Rug Creator", "scope": "archive-aware", "assistant_maker": true}, "links": {"related": ["Persian Rugs", "Oriental Rugs", "Area Rugs"], "sibling_edition": "rug"}}
{"id": "JAH-RUGS-000005", "slug": "rug-signature", "title": "Shag Rugs", "edition": "signature", "src": "signature-generated-completion", "built_by": "assistant-built", "record_kind": "rug record", "ladder_rank": 5, "body": "Signature-original. Shag rugs have a deep, long pile that feels soft underfoot. Pile height on shags can reach 2 inches or more, far deeper than standard cut-pile rugs. They suit bedrooms and living rooms but are poor choices for dining rooms, where chair legs sink and food spills hide. Vacuum shags with suction only — a beater bar can damage the long fibers. Shake them outdoors periodically to release trapped dust.", "capabilities": ["Define shag rug pile height", "Explain where shags work best", "Explain why shags suit bedrooms", "Describe correct shag vacuuming", "Explain outdoor shaking for dust"], "demo": {"language": "javascript", "title": "Pile depth comparison", "code": "const shag=2.0,standard=0.5;J({ratio:shag/standard});assert(shag/standard===4,'pile');", "verified_output": "{\"ratio\":4}", "verified_at": "2026-10-21", "node": "v24.20.0", "run": "node"}, "provenance": {"source_paste": "manons-orders-2026-10-20-database-batch.txt (items 129-131) + field-audit fill", "last_verified": "2026-10-21", "origin": "assistant-built"}, "million_march": {"target": 1000000, "records_now": 8, "status": "march-in-progress"}, "generator": {"hard_cap": 1000000000000000, "ladder": ["simple", "competitive", "mix-and-match", "unmade", "top-notch-or-better", "future-grade", "god-mode"], "self_regulation": true, "stop_when_complete": true}, "ai": {"name": "Signature Rug Creator", "scope": "archive-aware", "assistant_maker": true}, "links": {"related": ["Persian Rugs", "Oriental Rugs", "Area Rugs"], "sibling_edition": "rug"}}
{"id": "JAH-RUGS-000006", "slug": "rug-signature", "title": "Braided Rugs", "edition": "signature", "src": "signature-generated-completion", "built_by": "assistant-built", "record_kind": "rug record", "ladder_rank": 6, "body": "Signature-original. Braided rugs are made by braiding strips of fabric or yarn into long ropes, then coiling and stitching the ropes into ovals or rounds. They originated as a thrifty way to reuse worn clothing and feed sacks. Cotton, wool, and synthetic braided rugs are common; many are reversible. Because they are flat and flexible, braided rugs suit kitchens and casual rooms. Most braided rugs can be spot-cleaned, and many cotton ones are machine washable.", "capabilities": ["Explain how braided rugs are constructed", "Describe the origin of braided rugs", "List common braided rug materials", "Explain why braided rugs suit kitchens", "Describe braided rug cleaning"], "demo": {"language": "javascript", "title": "Braid length estimate", "code": "const strips=120,stripLen=36;const ropeLen=strips*stripLen/12;J({rope_feet:ropeLen});assert(ropeLen===360,'braid');", "verified_output": "{\"rope_feet\":360}", "verified_at": "2026-10-21", "node": "v24.20.0", "run": "node"}, "provenance": {"source_paste": "manons-orders-2026-10-20-database-batch.txt (items 129-131) + field-audit fill", "last_verified": "2026-10-21", "origin": "assistant-built"}, "million_march": {"target": 1000000, "records_now": 8, "status": "march-in-progress"}, "generator": {"hard_cap": 1000000000000000, "ladder": ["simple", "competitive", "mix-and-match", "unmade", "top-notch-or-better", "future-grade", "god-mode"], "self_regulation": true, "stop_when_complete": true}, "ai": {"name": "Signature Rug Creator", "scope": "archive-aware", "assistant_maker": true}, "links": {"related": ["Persian Rugs", "Oriental Rugs", "Area Rugs"], "sibling_edition": "rug"}}
{"id": "JAH-RUGS-000007", "slug": "rug-signature", "title": "Natural Fiber Rugs — Jute and Sisal", "edition": "signature", "src": "signature-generated-completion", "built_by": "assistant-built", "record_kind": "rug record", "ladder_rank": 7, "body": "Signature-original. Jute rugs are woven from soft plant fibers; they are inexpensive, earthy-looking, and best in low-traffic, dry rooms. Sisal is a stiffer agave fiber that wears very well and suits hallways and offices. Seagrass rugs are smooth and naturally stain-resistant but cannot get very wet. Natural fiber rugs should not be steam-cleaned — excess water causes shrinkage and browning. Layering a smaller patterned rug over a large jute rug is a popular decorating technique.", "capabilities": ["Compare jute, sisal, and seagrass", "Explain where jute rugs belong", "Explain why steam cleaning harms natural fibers", "Describe the layering technique", "List natural fiber rug materials"], "demo": {"language": "javascript", "title": "Layering size check", "code": "const base=[96,120],top=[60,84];const ok=top[0]<base[0]&&top[1]<base[1];J({fits:ok});assert(ok,'layer');", "verified_output": "{\"fits\":true}", "verified_at": "2026-10-21", "node": "v24.20.0", "run": "node"}, "provenance": {"source_paste": "manons-orders-2026-10-20-database-batch.txt (items 129-131) + field-audit fill", "last_verified": "2026-10-21", "origin": "assistant-built"}, "million_march": {"target": 1000000, "records_now": 8, "status": "march-in-progress"}, "generator": {"hard_cap": 1000000000000000, "ladder": ["simple", "competitive", "mix-and-match", "unmade", "top-notch-or-better", "future-grade", "god-mode"], "self_regulation": true, "stop_when_complete": true}, "ai": {"name": "Signature Rug Creator", "scope": "archive-aware", "assistant_maker": true}, "links": {"related": ["Persian Rugs", "Oriental Rugs", "Area Rugs"], "sibling_edition": "rug"}}
{"id": "JAH-RUGS-000008", "slug": "rug-signature", "title": "Rug Care, Cleaning, and Placement", "edition": "signature", "src": "signature-generated-completion", "built_by": "assistant-built", "record_kind": "rug record", "ladder_rank": 8, "body": "Signature-original. Vacuum rugs weekly, and rotate them 180 degrees once or twice a year so wear and sunlight stay even. Blot spills immediately — never rub, which spreads the stain and damages pile. Test any cleaner on a hidden corner first. Professional cleaning every 12 to 18 months keeps wool rugs in good shape. Keep rugs out of direct sun where possible, or expect gradual fading; rug pads extend rug life and protect floors.", "capabilities": ["Give a rug vacuuming schedule", "Explain the blot-don't-rub rule", "Explain rug rotation", "Describe professional cleaning intervals", "Explain how rug pads extend rug life"], "demo": {"language": "javascript", "title": "Rotation schedule", "code": "const months=[0,6,12,18];const rotations=months.filter(m=>m%6===0&&m>0).length;J({rotations_per_18mo:rotations});assert(rotations===3,'rotate');", "verified_output": "{\"rotations_per_18mo\":3}", "verified_at": "2026-10-21", "node": "v24.20.0", "run": "node"}, "provenance": {"source_paste": "manons-orders-2026-10-20-database-batch.txt (items 129-131) + field-audit fill", "last_verified": "2026-10-21", "origin": "assistant-built"}, "million_march": {"target": 1000000, "records_now": 8, "status": "march-in-progress"}, "generator": {"hard_cap": 1000000000000000, "ladder": ["simple", "competitive", "mix-and-match", "unmade", "top-notch-or-better", "future-grade", "god-mode"], "self_regulation": true, "stop_when_complete": true}, "ai": {"name": "Signature Rug Creator", "scope": "archive-aware", "assistant_maker": true}, "links": {"related": ["Persian Rugs", "Oriental Rugs", "Area Rugs"], "sibling_edition": "rug"}}
